  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is a safety setting, there is a way to see the avatar stats, how come I can find an avatar with literally 2458100000 particles, and it is not banned, or is just allowed in the game ? You can already attest that avatars have billions of particles, which are mostly used to crash people, with such an amount, how come you allow it to be uploaded ? How come such a thing can exist when yourself acknowledge it is far over the 5000 mark ?? Some avatars have no malicious intent in them, and are going far over your ratings, and that I can fully understand, the amount of polygons is pretty low for it to go from good to very poor, but you can't tell me a person isn't sus when their avatar has more than a billion² particles. Wouldn't that be easier to set at least a hard limit on the number of particles, at least, one that is not so high i don't even know what word to use to even talk about that number? That's how you suppress 50% of crashers for ya",
